  "title": "Haze4K Observable Conditional Utility-Risk Feasibility v1",
  "rationale": "Qualify one materially new contextual utility-risk head without reopening the failed weighted-ridge family or consuming protected confirmation data. The official ConvIR-B backbone remains frozen. A five-fold original-clear-scene OOF design on the 600 Haze4K training-role scenes estimates deployable spatial utility; the separate 150-scene train internal-development role supplies fixed calibration only; and the already exposed 100-scene Haze4K test-development role supplies a frozen-candidate stress test. The contract preserves the 0.05 dB utility margin and 0.025 dB precision target, counts no haze variant or tile as an independent sample, and permits a PASS to authorize only ITS/OTS cross-domain contract authoring.",
  "first_operation": "HAZE4K_OBSERVABLE_CONDITIONAL_UTILITY_RISK_QUALIFY",
